{"reference":"Psalms 1","packet_id":"commentary-v1.2-packet:b640b9d204f912fc39cb7213977739b881224a0f113a05e030ca21f1541401eb","prompt_version":"1.2","evidence_hash":"faf60db8a7de36c4d00e951e3171a6e49e875a4f98f9cba12be3cd2bca9465f8","synthesis_hash":"96e6e3b7925719c8329091c54d84981b935af1b459020c314b2813b9f8bbb82a","renderer_label":"Luna Medium","response_payload":{"reference":"Psalms 1","book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"cultural_context","title":"Cultural Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Ancient legal and treaty traditions provide background, but torah is distinct because it is the instruction of the covenant LORD rather than a generic code.","evidence_ids":["what-does-torah-mean:ancient_near_east_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_cultural_context_1d8147a28371"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-3"]},{"id":"block_2","text":"Israel shares wisdom forms with neighboring cultures, but anchors wisdom in covenant loyalty and the fear of the LORD.","evidence_ids":["what-is-biblical-wisdom:ancient_near_east_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_cultural_context_571303f56272"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-6"]},{"id":"block_3","text":"Poetic prayer was common in the ancient world, but the Psalms uniquely bind emotion to covenant faith.","evidence_ids":["what-is-a-psalm:ancient_near_east_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_cultural_context_da558b1104fe"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-6"]}]},{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Historical Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_4","text":"In Israel's story, torah names the covenant instruction given through Moses and the way the redeemed people are to live before God.","evidence_ids":["what-does-torah-mean:historical_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_historical_context_3bda7c5c94ff"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-3"]},{"id":"block_5","text":"Psalms arise in Israel's worship life and are sung in both public and private devotion.","evidence_ids":["what-is-a-psalm:historical_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_historical_context_74a20bc6440c"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-6"]},{"id":"block_6","text":"Wisdom literature grew from family instruction, court life, and worship, then became a major way Scripture teaches faithful living.","evidence_ids":["what-is-biblical-wisdom:historical_context:0"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_historical_context_dbadc6d62835"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"fact","verse_refs":["Psalms 1:1-6"]}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Surrounding Passages","blocks":[{"id":"block_7","text":"Psalms 1 and 2 form an untitled gateway that places Torah-shaped flourishing, the way of the wicked, rebellious nations, YHWH's kingship, and the anointed king before the collection.","evidence_ids":["psalms-gateway-torah-king"],"synthesis_ids":["syn_surrounding_passages_cf0c8bcc49ac"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed","verse_refs":[]}]}],"generated_metadata":null}}
